From 29ec667ba2ce67e2ab01eff64448706b18be9705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:57:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/68] Sync the round 3/4 liveness engine; expose its metrics

Engine jars from Mosip26 ff66597 (person5-android rebased on the team main
with Part 3 rounds 3 and 4, plus PR #4); the model bundle is unchanged
(pad-2026.10.1, same SHA-256). What the app sees from rounds 3/4:
- DEVICE_ERROR is recoverable with Retry until the per-session device
  error limit (3) is exceeded, then FAILED_FINAL with the device code; the
  LivenessPage already shows Retry for a recoverable DEVICE_ERROR. The fake
  DEVICE_FAILURE scenario now follows the same pattern; no scenario was
  renamed.
- A one-challenge session (operator/supervisor default) is never BLINK
  alone when another type is usable; a BLINK-only pool is still honoured.
- The liveness-api contract is unchanged.

LivenessServiceHolder.metrics(useFake) returns the engine's
LivenessMetrics.Snapshot (DefaultLivenessService.metrics() /
FakeLivenessService.metrics(): anonymised counts, rates and averages, no
session ids, individual scores or images); debug builds log its toMap() at
the end of each session. CameraXFrameSource: PR #4's wording of the sync
script reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
